{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e465ed4fbaddf8e0b7baaacd93150b7221ed25124fa35e5a3aa1b2eb2708e476","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_6a836c426c4f3f07222251c18bb69c3d2325bbfc634ab9e06c7538dcf2e66ed4","overall_assessment":"The paper is well-organized with a logical flow from background to architecture improvements and classifier guidance. The writing is generally clear, though minor typographical errors and inconsistent notation in the pseudocode slightly reduce precision. The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined, and the tables are readable and informative.","paper_id":"OU98jZWS3x_","paper_identity_sha256":"a00a2fd867b87895703b34a264bc874191e36a013092754c36c4c794c3fc2cfb","prompt_identity_sha256":"55dac0a4d4514c71b15525c01d24345fe8dc8450bf36ba008ba11b8e8d758bbd","raw_response_sha256":"7207e543e02b2e8dd59a3215f9d20710e3e259513c83a7e5b1e734c205965b4a","request_identity_sha256":"3480ac3800eb553d7220be907dc8bde6aa85f87ad180fcd22ec3740048acc66a","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"a4db541c156c655b7f0d835f7987df0d9ad37041efb6bc58ec1bcc43b3602298","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-019"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured with a clear narrative flow from background to specific contributions. However, there are minor typographical errors that affect precision, such as the misspelling of 'convolutions' as 'colvolutions' in Section 3 and 'noisig' as 'noisig' in Section 4. Additionally, the notation in Algorithm 1 and 2 uses epsilon_theta(x_t) and p_phi(y|x_t) without the timestep t, which is later clarified in the text but could be more consistent in the pseudocode itself to avoid initial confusion.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-008","SRC-015"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. Key concepts such as the noise prediction function epsilon_theta(x_t, t), the variance parameterization Sigma_theta(x_t, t), and the adaptive group normalization layer AdaGN(h, y) are clearly introduced and used consistently throughout the paper. The derivations and explanations of the diffusion process and classifier guidance are mathematically sound and easy to follow.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-026"],"review_text":"The tables in the paper are readable and well-structured, providing clear comparisons of different architectural changes and their impact on FID. The captions for the tables are descriptive and help the reader understand the context of the data presented. The figure references are consistent, and the captions for the figures provide sufficient detail to understand the visual content without needing to see the images themselves.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"1fcc495a7e02ba7da6395e03bc1200dbba12c3e2764556c86a6b814b72f6c611","paper_id":"OU98jZWS3x_","paper_ordinal":113,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"7207e543e02b2e8dd59a3215f9d20710e3e259513c83a7e5b1e734c205965b4a","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"OU98jZWS3x_","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"b33baaed2721de2b0a12038fbbc60e7298a06bd3a154d2689fbdc65954291058","request_identity_sha256":"3480ac3800eb553d7220be907dc8bde6aa85f87ad180fcd22ec3740048acc66a","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":559,"prompt_tokens":19215,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19774},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"3480ac3800eb553d7220be907dc8bde6aa85f87ad180fcd22ec3740048acc66a","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}